    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is, and what it is not",
      "prov:value": "**A design record.** It states what was agreed for the folio board, in the CRDM\nrun on [issue #602](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/602)\nbetween 2026-09-20 and 2026-09-21, and it exists so that a person asking *why\nis the board shaped like this* has one place to look.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#602",
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is, and what it is not",
      "prov:value": "It is **history, not instruction**, and that is the line the owner drew: a\nskill carries what a competent practitioner needs *in order to do* the task,\nand everything past that — the reasoning, the options not taken, the\nmeasurements behind a threshold — is documentation. Every sentence below describes what was\nagreed on a date, against a repository in a state. Where the implementation has\nsince diverged, the divergence is stated rather than smoothed. Nothing here\ntells an agent what to do — the rules an agent follows live in the\n`cat-harness` skills this set produced, and the processes live in the three\nexecutable BPMN diagrams beside them.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner ruling"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is, and what it is not",
      "prov:value": "**Filed here on the owner's ruling, 2026-09-21:**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is, and what it is not",
      "prov:value": "> this is a memory asset as part of design, so it goes into docs/ […] this was\n> an asset as part of building a feature […] but it is not the content we want\n> displayed itself.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this is, and what it is not",
      "prov:value": "**And why it is in `cat-harness/docs/` specifically**, sharpened the same day:\n*\"if it is realated to some harness/feature/tool that detailed infromation/\ndesign/planning/etc go into that harness' docs/\"*. The board's schema and\nbehaviour live in `cat-harness` by the requester's own layering, so the record\nof why they are shaped that way lives in that instance's `docs/` — not in the\nrepository root's, and not in a folio's.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The need, in the requester's words",
      "prov:value": "The whole set derives from this, kept verbatim because the layering sentence is\nprecise and a paraphrase loses it:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "requester quote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The need, in the requester's words",
      "prov:value": "> landing folio should really be resizable, switchiing over to content avatars\n> if content no longer lgeible. liek miro board. content vieweing panes are\n> resizzble. but ALWAYS collapsable to linearly rendablee/just the docs. the\n> todos/miro board is a static content overlays, so new content type that sits\n> under todos/ but scema and behavhoir of folio=miro board is in cat-harness.\n> carefull separte tools and schema.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "requester quote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Round one — R1 to R7",
      "prov:value": "Agreed in Phase 3. Of the seven, **exactly one introduced a genuinely new\nmechanism**; that finding is why the implementation was ten small units rather\nthan one large one.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "Phase 3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R3",
      "prov:value": "This one was a **defect in something already published**. The value is\n`sec:<page>-<node>`, page-qualified for a good reason — the bare node id\n`what-is-not-built-yet` existed on two pages. But any consumer asking *which\npage is this note on* had to string-manipulate: know the `sec:` prefix, know\nthe separator is `-`, and know node ids themselves contain `-`, so the split is\nnot unambiguous without already holding the page list.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "targetLabel defect"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R3",
      "prov:value": "**Our own client escaped it by accident**, matching on the whole string and\nnever parsing, which is exactly why it went unnoticed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "client"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R4 — the linear floor",
      "prov:value": "As agreed, R4 read *reachable without JavaScript*. The board SHALL always be\ncollapsible to a linear rendering; movement SHALL be **keyboard-operable**,\nand drag MAY be an accelerator but SHALL NOT be the only way in — this\ninstance's declared interaction profile is low-dexterity.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "R4 original"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "R4 — the linear floor",
      "prov:value": "> **RELAXED by the owner, 2026-10-02**, verbatim:\n>\n> > relax...\"reachable without JavaScript\" to \"reachable without XSS\"\n>\n> So the floor is no longer *no JavaScript*. It is **no injected script**: the\n> board's linear rendering MAY fetch and build its content client-side, and\n> MUST NOT be reachable by anything that executes markup it did not author.\n>\n> **What the relaxation does NOT touch**, because the same paragraph states\n> them independently: movement stays keyboard-operable, and drag stays an\n> accelerator rather than the only way in. No byte-count argument reaches the\n> interaction profile.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R4 — the linear floor",
      "prov:value": "**The subject of that sentence is the board**, and saying so is a correction\nrather than a clarification. The relaxation was first recorded here with the\nmeasurement that prompted it — the docs site's `<nav>`, 87.7 KB of identical\nbytes in each of 2,023 published pages — presented as the reason a *board*\nrequirement had to move. It was not. Three facts settled it on 2026-10-02:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "R4 — the linear floor",
      "prov:value": "- **this document is not instruction** — §\"What this is, and what it is not\"\n  says so in the owner's own ruling, and the rules an agent follows live in\n  the `cat-harness` skills this set produced;\n- **the skill that does bind the docs site is**\n  [`ui-accessibility`](https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/reference/skill-instructions/ui-accessibility.html),\n  which binds \"the knowledge-graph viewer, the docs site, the action-icon\n  tiles, anything future\" to WCAG 2.2 A/AA, keyboard reachability, 24 px\n  targets, computed contrast, visible focus and announced change — **and\n  carries no no-JavaScript clause**, because WCAG imposes none;\n- **the docs navbar already requires JavaScript.** `mountNavIconRow`,\n  `mountDocumentIndex` and `mountInstanceGraphs` build three of its regions in\n  the DOM at load, shipped in #959, and no gate objects.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#959",
        "2026-10-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "R4 — the linear floor",
      "prov:value": "So the docs nav never stood on R4 and needed no relaxation to be loaded once.\nWhat the relaxation *does* reach is the artefact R4 names: the board's linear\nfloor is the todo listing, and the tools layer's `test/linear-floor.e2e.ts` is five\n`javaScriptEnabled: false` assertions over it. Relaxing R4 permits converting\nthat listing to a fetch; it does not decide whether to, and the test's header\nrecords what the static floor cost to build (bean `0jtj`: with JavaScript off,\na reader previously got \"no note, no count, no hint that notes exist\").",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0jtj"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "R4 — the linear floor",
      "prov:value": "**The two obligations a client-side rendering owes are rules, so they live in\nthe skill** — print and PDF wait for load and render before printing; a load\nthat fails says so rather than rendering as empty. Both were stated by the\nowner the same day, and both were first written *here*, in a document that\ndisclaims being instruction, where nothing enforces them and no agent looking\nfor the rule would find them. They are in\n[`ui-accessibility`](https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/reference/skill-instructions/ui-accessibility.html)\n§\"A rendering built client-side owes two things the static one gave for free\",\nwith the measurements and the `console.warn` trap. This entry is the history of\nhow they arrived, which is all this file is for.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner, same day"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Round two — R8 to R14",
      "prov:value": "These arrived **after** the requirements gateway had closed, and were checked\nagainst the declared model rather than assumed compatible. They are additive:\nnothing already agreed was invalidated.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "requirements gateway"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "R15 and R16 — reconstructed, then confirmed",
      "prov:value": "**They were referenced but never written down.** Bean `51wf` is assigned\n*\"R2, R9, R15\"* and bean `zsah` *\"R12, R16\"*, and no comment on #602 states\neither requirement. When this record was first written they were therefore\nreported as **undefined**, with the recoverable meaning marked as inference —\nbecause a design record that fills its own gaps with plausible sentences is\nworse than one that names them, since invented text reads exactly like agreed\ntext.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 51wf",
        "bean zsah",
        "#602"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "R15 and R16 — reconstructed, then confirmed",
      "prov:value": "**The owner confirmed both readings on 2026-09-21** (*\"agreed on r15/16\"*), so\nthey are now agreed requirements rather than reconstructions:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R15 and R16 — reconstructed, then confirmed",
      "prov:value": "Both were implemented to that reading before it was confirmed, which is why the\ngap mattered: the code was already committed to an interpretation nothing had\nstated. **The provenance is kept rather than tidied away** — a requirement\nrecovered from a bean's unit description and later ratified is not the same\nartefact as one written down at the time, and a reader re-checking this\nsubsystem should know which it is.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "provenance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Round three — R18 to R32",
      "prov:value": "These arrived on 2026-09-21, after R1–R17 had shipped and while `v0jv`'s tile\ndock was still unmerged. They are the first round that is **about the folio as\na surface** rather than about the board's mechanics, and two of them corrected\nwork that had not yet landed — which is why they are recorded as a round rather\nthan folded into the requirements they revise. Reading them as amendments would\nlose the fact that a shipped-to-branch design was turned round before a reader\never saw it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean v0jv",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Geometry — R18 to R23",
      "prov:value": "**R23 reverses `v0jv`, and that bean's own text says why the reversal was\navailable.** `v0jv` quoted the owner as *\"stacked around (bottom?) of folio\"* —\nthe parenthesis and the question mark are the requester's, and were carried\ninto the bean verbatim precisely because they marked an open question rather\nthan a decision. The dock was built to the bottom, closed, and R23 settles both\nhalves the other way: **top**, and **open by default**. The default is the half\nthat would have shipped silently — tiles a reader must open before they can see\nwhat a folio offers read as absent, which is the complaint `v0jv` itself opened\nwith about the in-flow row.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean v0jv"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The folio is a convention, not a page — R24 to R29",
      "prov:value": "Paraphrased: these requirements are really for how the \"folio\" visualisation\nfrom cat-harness should work, and by convention it should be available on any\nharness for a consistent feel. The content layers (the IRIS replica, the SMART\nIGs and so on) are libraries a user browses, and the cat-harness \"folio\" is\nconsistent across them; todos and the like can reference the cross-KG library.\nA content layer may implement its own landing page or have its own harness.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "requester paraphrase"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "An asset has three states, not two — R30",
      "prov:value": "Clarified in a follow-up the same day, and it is the requirement most likely to\nbe implemented as two states by somebody reading quickly:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "An asset has three states, not two — R30",
      "prov:value": "**Why three rather than two.** A two-state model — *in the folio* or *not* —\nmakes closing a sticky and un-materialising an asset the same gesture, so a\nreader tidying their glass silently discards work. The middle state is what\nmakes closing safe: the asset stays in `folio/`, and the way back onto the\nglass is *\"go back to the library and pull it out\"*. That is also `l4zi`\napplied one level up — the inverse of **close** must be reachable, and here it\nis reachable from a different surface than the one that closed it, which is a\nthing a design can get wrong without any single screen looking wrong.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean l4zi"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A sticky's face — R31 and R32",
      "prov:value": "**R31 rejected the recommendation that was put to the owner**, which had been a\nhidden accessible label alongside the visible summary. The reason given is the\nbetter one and is worth keeping: *\"that's new data to maintain\"* — a second\nstring is a second thing that can drift from the first, and a hidden label that\ndisagrees with the visible text is a defect no reader can see. Condensing the\ntext the sticky already carries has no such failure mode.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**It was recorded here as undefined**, and deliberately: *\"OR use theme/avatars\nas appropriate\"* named a choice that nothing in the corpus said how to make,\nand a rule invented to close the gap reads exactly like a rule that was agreed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "R19 undefined"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**The owner settled it on 2026-09-21**, choosing declaration ownership from\nfour options put to them:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**R19c is the owner's correction to R19b, the same day**, and it is recorded\nas its own requirement rather than folded in because R19b is still true and\nstill insufficient:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**The empty asymmetry was already half-written too.** `head_custom.html`\nrecords the content side — *\"a board that opens empty is indistinguishable\nfrom a person with nothing outstanding, and those are opposite facts\"* — while\n`pb04` covers the functional side: an affordance that promises and delivers\nnothing.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean pb04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**The provenance is kept rather than tidied away**, the same as R15/R16: this\nis a rule recovered by argument and then ratified, not one written down at the\ntime, and a reader re-checking the board should know which it is.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "provenance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**Two candidate rules were falsified by R30 before the choice was put.** R30\nplaces *\"avatars of materialized assets (including materialized KG like\nbootstrap, cat-harness)\"* on the glass — so a **whole knowledge graph renders\nas an avatar**. That kills *\"many behind it → tile\"* outright, and it kills\n*\"opens a viewer over a set → tile\"* too, since opening that avatar does open\na viewer over a set. Declaration ownership survives because a materialised\nasset is in the reader's `folio/` **however big it is**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "options put"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-33",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "R19's second clause — reported open, then settled the same day",
      "prov:value": "**It is recognition rather than invention**, which is the reason to prefer it:\n`harness-tiles` already carried *\"a tile is the harness's, not the node's\"*,\nand the owner's own 2026-09-20 line — *\"if harness declares visaluzers, those\nshould have tile. defaults to theme, but new can be changed\"* — already said\nboth halves. The gap was that nobody had read them as an answer to this\nquestion.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-34",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "R27 and question 1 — answered by the corpus, then settled",
      "prov:value": "**The requester's own parenthetical marked this unsettled**: *\"clarifying if\nKG is static w// materizlied…\"*. Measured 2026-09-21, the answer was already\nin the corpus in three places, none of which had been read as answering it:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-35",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the bytes land — the part that DID need deciding",
      "prov:value": "R27 says *\"materialized should live in folio\"*, and the IRIS replica materialises\ninto `library/` (items and covers) and `uploads/` (source PDFs). **Neither is\n`folio/`.** Three readings were put to the owner; they chose **the folio is\nthe reader's REPOSITORY**, of which `library/` and `uploads/` are already\ndeclared parts:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner chose repository reading"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-36",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the bytes land — the part that DID need deciding",
      "prov:value": "`dependents: \"reproduce\"` (retired 2026-09-30; now the `perInstance` flag on the kind) was the schema saying **this is the reader's own\ncopy** — the exact fact R27 reaches for, and it predates R27.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-37",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the bytes land — the part that DID need deciding",
      "prov:value": "**The literal reading would have broken a consumer, and that was found AFTER\nthe options were tabled.** It is recorded here for that reason rather than\nfolded into the argument as though it had been known.\n`schemas/materialization.ts` states it outright — ***`corpus-grep` searches\n`library/` only***, so a node materialised into `folio/` would read as ABSENT\nto every consumer. That is the same defect the schema forbids one state up,\nwhere collapsing `referenced` into `materialized` hides a node nobody holds.\nHad the owner chosen the literal reading, it would have been a migration into\na known breakage, and the recommendation put alongside the options did not say\nso because this had not been measured yet.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "found after options tabled"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-38",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where the bytes land — the part that DID need deciding",
      "prov:value": "**R27 is therefore already satisfied, and already gated.**\nthe content core's `scripts/check-catalogue.ts` checks that a `materialized` claim names\nbytes that exist, with `local-path.ts`'s three states (`ok` / `missing` /\n`unknown`) and bean `yl5w`'s scar behind it: *three claims resolved to nothing\nand the gate said clean*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean yl5w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-39",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "**The library view already renders all three states — this was recorded here\nas open twice, and both were wrong** (bean `mm36`, measured 2026-09-22).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean mm36",
        "2026-09-22"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-40",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "**The first look was misleading and the trap is worth recording**: the source\ntree holds three committed the IRIS replica's `docs/` pages and the badges appear on\nonly one of them — `kg-to-portal.html`, the *legend*. The catalogue pages are\ngenerated at build time, so a source-tree grep says \"almost nowhere\" about\nsomething that is in fact everywhere. **This had to be measured on the\npublished site.**",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "source-tree grep"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-41",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "The owner's own words are in that generator's header and are about exactly\nthis — *\"collectiosn w/ nothing greyed out\"* — with the reasoning beside them:\n*\"a row that says **referenced** reads as 'upstream, not here', which is the\nactual state and the distinction the whole catalogue-by-reference model is\nfor.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner quote"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-42",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "**F8/F9 is blocked on R25, structurally rather than by scheduling** — bean\n`jpjt`, settled 2026-09-21.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean jpjt",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-43",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "The gap is measured: on the deployed preview the IRIS replica's `index.html` loads\n`docs-ui.js` **0** times and carries **0** boards and **0** tiles, against\n9 / 1 / 28 on the folio-assistant landing page. A reader browsing that library\nhas **no folio at all**, not a degraded one.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "preview measurement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-44",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "**The delivery mechanism is decided** — three ways were tabled and the owner\nchose an **exported mount fragment plus a gate**, the shape\n`staging-banner.ts` already proves, reusing `bodyInsertionPoint()` so that\n`ur84` cannot recur.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "owner chose",
        "bean ur84"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-45",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Still open from this round",
      "prov:value": "Both tracked on\n[issue #796](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/issues/796).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#796"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-46",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where this diverged from what was agreed",
      "prov:value": "One place, and it is recorded on the bean as well.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 51wf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "docs/concepts/architecture/folio-board-requirements.md#provenance-47",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Where this diverged from what was agreed",
      "prov:value": "`51wf`'s checklist said *\"every card starts as its avatar, at any size\"*, which\ncannot be literal alongside R2 — if cards are avatars at every width, R2 has\nnothing to do. It was read as **\"starts closed\"**: a closed card shows its words\nabove the declared threshold and its avatar below it, with the avatar present at\nevery width as the control that opens the window. Flagged rather than silently\nchosen, and **confirmed by the owner on 2026-09-21**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 51wf",
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
